    "tree_id": "27cb652f0225c7158ccec7c73f9d2cdb696ade60",
    "message": "Use KERN_PROC_PID and run the syntax gate in a venv\n\nThe first macOS compile found one error: the debugger check asked for\nKERN_PID, which Darwin does not define, so NABATIAppIntegrity.swift never\ncompiled. KERN_PROC_PID is the constant for \"this process\".\n\nThe syntax step also reported success without parsing anything: the runner's\npython3 is PEP 668 externally managed, so pip refused the install and the tool\nprinted SKIP. It now installs into build/venv, so the grammar is real.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-12T12:01:35Z",
    "author": {
      "name": "thait2471-sys",
      "email": "thait2471@gmail.com"
    },
    "committer": {
      "name": "thait2471-sys",
      "email": "thait2471@gmail.com"
    }
  },
